  "summary_en": "UN Secretary-General's report under GA resolution 78/241 consolidating Member State and observer views on lethal autonomous weapons systems, with annexed submissions from States, ICRC and civil society. It covers definitions, humanitarian, legal and ethical concerns, and next steps. The Secretary-General reiterates the call for a legally binding instrument by 2026.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No agreed international definition of LAWS; many States stress meaningful human control over the use of force.",
   "Many States support the two-tier approach: prohibit systems that cannot comply with IHL, regulate the rest.",
   "States are divided on a new legally binding instrument versus reliance on existing IHL; the CCW GGE is the main forum.",
   "The Secretary-General calls for a legally binding instrument by 2026 banning LAWS that operate without human control.",
   "Annexes reproduce the submissions of States, the ICRC and civil society in their original language."
  ],
